    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0091" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/300</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commercial Adviser of
                        the British Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Crawford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Richard</hi>: I have your letter of March
                    23, 1918, in which you inquire the views of this Government in regard to Russian
                    funds in this country. Up to the present time the status of Mr. Boris
                    Bakhmeteff, as Ambassador, representing the Provisional Government of Russia,
                    and the propriety of his controlling such funds as may be available to him in
                    this country in that capacity have not been questioned.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
